cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "no-model-floor: checking whether a safety benchmark measures the model"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Lovell
    given-names: Jason
abstract: >-
  This software checks whether an adaptive safety benchmark measures the model or a
  surrounding scaffold. It provides two diagnostics: replace the model with fixed
  policies and re-score the complete system, then measure the gap between the best
  shared control setting and settings selected per unit. In the included synthetic
  study, a fixed policy scores full marks and the declared control family has zero
  adaptation headroom under the stated metric conditions. Committed analyses also
  report no-model floors for third-party classification benchmarks, but the external
  corpora are not redistributed and those aggregate results require separate
  reproduction and statistical review. The work does not establish held-out adaptive
  benefit or a general result about safety benchmarks. The portable implementation in
  floors.py has no runtime dependencies.
keywords:
  - agent safety
  - evaluation methodology
  - benchmark validity
  - ablation
  - local language models
license: MIT
